{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"BEDROCK CUTOVER MEASURED END-TO-END. A real plan-review ran on bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6\nagainst closed ticket 7468: 19 LLM calls, verdict BLOCK with a substantive plan-specific finding,\nZERO provider errors, zero degradations, no LLMUnavailableError. The provider path is functionally\nsound. But THREE blockers were measured, and two of them I re-verified myself.\n\n1. NO SINGLE-SCALAR SETTING REPRODUCES TODAY'S SPLIT. Baseline (direct Anthropic) = 41 opus (Pass-1)\n   + 1 sonnet (Pass-2/4). The Bedrock run = 0 opus, 19 sonnet. REBAR_LLM_MODEL drives EVERY pass, so:\n     - point it at Bedrock sonnet -> Pass-1 drops opus->sonnet, a CAPABILITY REGRESSION and a direct\n       violation of the operator's 'Pass-1 opus-equivalent' requirement;\n     - point it at Bedrock opus  -> Pass-2/Pass-4 lose the cost downgrade AND greedy decoding.\n   => cc33 (class consumption at the runner) is a HARD PREREQUISITE for this story. Cutting over\n   before it lands silently degrades review quality either way.\n\n2. THE VERIFIER DOWNGRADE IS DEAD ON EVERY NON-BARE MODEL ID. I re-ran the pure function myself:\n     claude-opus-4-8                        -> Pass-2 claude-sonnet-4-6                  downgraded=True\n     anthropic:claude-opus-4-8              -> Pass-2 anthropic:claude-opus-4-8          downgraded=False\n     bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8   -> Pass-2 bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8 downgraded=False\n   verify.py:269 only downgrades on an EXACT match against the bare 'claude-opus-4-8'. Note the\n   middle row: merely QUALIFYING the same model with its provider kills the downgrade. This is wider\n   than Bedrock.\n\n3. ESCALATION CROSSES PROVIDERS. I re-verified: models_at_or_above('bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6')\n   returns [('claude-sonnet-4-6','anthropic'), ('claude-opus-4-8','anthropic')] — BARE ids that infer\n   to provider 'anthropic'. On a context-limit error a Bedrock run silently escalates to DIRECT\n   ANTHROPIC: a hard failure in a Bedrock-only container with no key, or silent Anthropic billing\n   where a key exists. Not triggered in the run (no context-limit hit) — confirmed from the function,\n   not observed live.\n\nTWO FINDINGS THAT FAVOUR THE CUTOVER:\n- PROMPT CACHING WORKS ON BEDROCK for both sonnet and opus (raw converse: cacheWrite then cacheRead\n  on a repeated prefix; through rebar end-to-end: cache_read=542,723 / cache_write=6,239 over 19\n  calls). Bug 7a79's silent no-op is a DIRECT-ANTHROPIC-path problem — Bedrock FIXES it rather than\n  inheriting it. That is a cost argument for the cutover.\n- TEMPERATURE: Bedrock sonnet accepts temperature=0.0; Bedrock opus rejects any value except the\n  default 1.0 ('temperature is deprecated for this model'). So what is deprecated is TUNABILITY, not\n  the parameter. rebar already withdraws it via capabilities overrides so opus will not crash — but\n  the greedy Pass-2 pin (temperature: 0) is then silently INOPERATIVE. Keeping the verifier on\n  SONNET preserves greedy verification; that is now a measured argument, not a preference."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785496008457105001,"uuid":"ebf77324-a446-4d9e-9ac4-c7b8b0e9da79"}